`var` is function-scoped, so all three callbacks close over the same single `i`. The `setTimeout` callbacks run after the loop finishes, when `i` has already been incremented to 3 (the value that failed `i < 3`), so each logs 3.

Fix: use `let`, which creates a fresh binding per iteration.

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
```

The older fix is an IIFE (`(j => setTimeout(() => console.log(j), 0))(i)`) or `setTimeout(console.log, 0, i)`, which passes the current value as an argument.
